 have  to wait to find out why that was  we do see his rageful reaction that  involves smashing the receiver and  kicking in the glass for good measure  because this is so extreme i think it  only makes sense that he did talk to her  and as frustrating as it is not to know  what was said the effect it has on him  is what really matters after kim left we  found out that he became saul as a way  to cope with everything that happened we  know jimmy never dealt with chuck's or  howard's deaths and that he tries to  forget about what happened with kim by  throwing himself into being the criminal  lawyer saul goodman after episode 609  that put a sad spin on the character's  existence during breaking bad but this  episode makes things more complicated i  already mentioned him ignoring mike's  warning about walt and what that brought  to mind was the switch in his office in  the first episode of season 2. that made  the point that when he gets something in  his mind he can't help himself and they  jump back and forth between the two  timelines to really drive this idea home  in omaha he's reeling from whatever kim  told him on the phone and so he heads  back to jeff's where he shows marion how  to watch funny cat videos on her new  laptop i thought the way odenkirk played  gene here was really telling he's  laughing with her one minute but gets  deadly serious when he tells jeff they  should take their drinks outside he  needs to throw himself into this as fast  as possible to drown out his thoughts of  kim the scams start off feeling fun in  the same way that nippy was he appears  to pick marks that aren't nice people  and especially the first one feels like  he might even have it coming to him he  uses the name victor with a k and it  feels like he might be chasing some of  what he got out of those early scams  with gisele we see that he has things  planned out he has jeff take the night  shift and obtain some barbiturates gene  finds guys he can befriend at bars while  pretending to get drunk with them and  then have jeff drug them with  complimentary water on the way home he  uses a piece of tape to leave their  doors unlocked so that buddy can come in  behind him and steal their identities  while they're knocked out they sell  their information for a decent payday  and then do it all again in albuquerque  it's been a few years since kim left so  at this point he's just chasing a bigger  high after his post kidnap conversation  where he put it together that walter is  heisenberg he sees an opportunity i  suppose that some people might look at  this as saul being responsible for who  walter white will become but i think  that is missing the point of who  heisenberg was we have two stories about  two different journeys so i look at this  as it being what happens when they come  together and i've always thought of  their transformations as being unique to  each other but at least at the end of  this episode they're looking a lot more  similar because things do get dark  quickly in omaha as gene starts to  resemble saul a lot more than jimmy he  was already wearing the pinky ring and  he adds a bluetooth headset and the back  massager and he starts sleeping with sex  workers again there's a moment when he  realizes that one of his marks has  cancer where you think he might pump on  the brakes but it goes in the opposite  direction he gets a call and rushes over  to jeff's because buddy couldn't go  through with his part of the robbery he  noticed that their mark took the same  cancer meds his dad was taking and  decides not to steal from him gene flips  out and tries to convince him that he'll  get over it and when that doesn't work  he decides to do it himself  there's a great shot on the way to the  house with jeff looking at gene in his  rear view mirror where you can see that  he's really afraid of him at this point  it's a complete 180 from when he was  first in his cab and it underlines how  quickly and completely that gene went  off the rails everything about this  decision to go to the house is  compulsive it's been long enough that  the barbiturates may no longer be  working buddy removed the tape so he  won't be able to walk right in and when  he breaks the window that undermines the  entire purpose of the scam they were  going to great lengths to make sure  these guys wouldn't realize they'd been  robbed and as the episode comes to an  end we know that won't be the case this  time and as they've done throughout the  episode they cut back and forth between  the two timelines and there's a great  parallel of him walking into walt's high  school here with what gene does at the  end of this episode the decision to go  to walt and to tell him he has the right  product but not the right connections  and strategy and then offer to provide  him those things it was the beginning of  the end for saul goodman it makes this  final decision to go after this other  cancer man feel like it could be the end  of gene so careful what you wish for  this episode gave us answers and the  return of walt and jesse but it made the  jimmy's side winning the battle for his  soul feel less likely they were almost  hitting us over the head with the  similarities between the fall assault  goodman and the end of gene takabic in  both of those situations he was making  decisions and chasing after what he was  wishing for and we know what that's  about now and at least in the breaking  bad timeline we know how that worked out  i really liked how they managed the  jumping back and forth and the  transition of the grave in the desert to  him awakened the bed he made for himself  in omaha really sticks with you there's  an incredible amount of references like  the gas station where francesca gets the  call is the same one where jesse gave  the girl to counter meth and speaking of  that the whole find the rock shaped like  new jersey and follow the fishing line  to the drainpipe was fun to watch i  don't know if i needed the answer to  what happened to huel but i was happy  when i got it and i read in the  hollywood reporter that thomas now said  that he named price daniel because he  was hoping to make him the danny from  the laser tag and they never got around  to it so he was excited to slip that in  during the call and make it official i  also saw several posts that pointed out  that he was pictured on one of the  driver's licenses during the montage as  we become used to with this show and i  would say in his episodes in particular  it was a heavy episode with just the  right amount of funny moments included  to balance things out there were so many  things in the crystal ship you had him  asking if oakley came out the massage  machine itself and mike's reaction to it  francesca as a landlord marian with  funny cat videos and i'm not sure if it  was supposed to be funny but i did find  buddy's incredibly well-behaved dog to  be a nice touch it's not like this is a  surprise but i have to mention the  performances watching odenkirk play saul  and possibly showing us a new sided gene  after the phone call it's wild how each  one of these different versions of jimmy  comes across cranston and paul with the  aid of some beanies seem to slip right  back into their roles i think if i had  to choose a favorite moment it would be  jesse saying dick under his breath but  walt's lecture about how they just need  to let it cool down is right up there  with it the last thing i got that i  really wanted was to see gene and kim  reconnect and i would have never guessed  that it could lead to him putting  himself on this path because we didn't  hear what they said and because we don't  know what she's up to i feel pretty  confident that we're gonna see this same  conversation from her side in the next  episode she is working at a store that  sells sprinklers and it's titled  waterworks based on the timing it's  possible she just learned what he was up  to with walt it stands out though that  he thought he knew where she worked he  was able to call the operator and get in  touch with her just like that it's hard  to say where we go in the timeline from  here it doesn't necessarily feel like we  need to revisit anything with walt and  jesse although i wouldn't mind it but  him having this information makes it  seem like it's at least possible that  they got together at least once during  the breaking bad timeline what they said  and whether that happened or if he just  had someone go find her all of that  being a mystery means that we really  have no idea how she'd be feeling about  him as far as the way things were left  after episode 609 it's safe to say that  she still cares about him she doesn't  believe that they can be together but  she wouldn't want him to be suffering  either considering she knows what he's  been through and she knows him better  than anyone else she may understand what  he's doing with this saul goodman  persona at the very least she  understands that him burying all these  unresolved feelings about chuck about  howard that none of that's good for him  but without knowing what she's facing in  her own life it's hard to imagine how  those two things will influence each  other if there's any chance that he  turns things around because at the end  of this episode he looks set up to go  down in a blaze of glory similar to mr  walter white i never envisioned that as  an ending for him so i'm interested to  see if there's a way that he can resolve  that if he can move past that and  there's still two more full episodes to  go to see if he does and i think that is  a great place to leave things let me  know in the comments what you thought  about the episode i think tom sniles  went out on a high note i wouldn't say  that this episode topped bad choice road  or planet execution but i think that's  more about where they fell in the story  and what was going on then about  anything he did in this particular  episode next week we're gonna see the  last episode directed by vince gilligan  and then one more that's written and  directed by the showrunner peter gold so  let me know what you hope to see happen  how you think it might end and what you  definitely don't want to see please like  this video if you enjoyed it please  subscribe to my channel if you haven't  already and thanks for watching i'll  talk to you soon  you


